meta {
  name: Days
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{api}}/bonds/{{bondId}}/days?limit=20
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  limit: 20
  ~until: 2026-10-09
  ~favourites: true
  ~cursor: {{nextCursor}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    const first = res.body.items[0];
    if (first) {
      bru.setVar("date", first.date);
      if (first.partnerEntry) bru.setVar("partnerEntryId", first.partnerEntry.id);
    }
    if (res.body.nextCursor) bru.setVar("nextCursor", res.body.nextCursor);
  }
}

docs {
  The archive, newest day first: every day you have something to see on. A day is your entry, your partner's, and the day's status; each entry you can read says whether YOU have marked it (favourited).

  Three parameters are switched off here; tick one to send it. until starts the page at that date or the nearest earlier one. favourites=true keeps to the days holding an entry you have marked. cursor is the nextCursor of the page before: it is kept when a response carries one, and null means there is no earlier page. A value the server cannot read is 422, naming the parameter.

  The first day's date and your partner's entry on it are kept for Day, Favourite and Unfavourite.
}
